# Squire home server — compose stack config (SQUIRE-T-0129).
#   cp .env.example .env      (deploy/.env is gitignored — it holds your Tailscale auth key)

# --- Pairing address (REQUIRED) -------------------------------------------
# The host phones are told to reach this server at — it is baked into every pairing QR. Inside a
# container the server cannot detect it (it would find Docker's bridge IP), so say it here.
#   * Home Wi-Fi only:  this computer's LAN IP, e.g. 192.168.1.50 (give it a DHCP reservation).
#   * With Tailscale:   the node's tailnet name or IP — e.g. squire.your-tailnet.ts.net, or the
#     100.x.y.z address from `tailscale status`. Phones paired with this address work at home AND
#     away, but only while Tailscale is connected on the phone. Use the full MagicDNS name; the
#     short name (`squire`) does not resolve reliably on Android.
# A phone that is ALREADY paired keeps the address it was paired with; re-pair it to move it over.
SQUIRE_PAIR_HOST=

# --- Ports ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The phone API. ONE number for the LAN and the tailnet (see docker-compose.yml). Moving an
# existing bare-metal install into the container? Keep ITS port — paired phones have it stored.
#SQUIRE_API_PORT=8080
# Host interface the API is published on. 0.0.0.0 = the LAN (phones at home). 127.0.0.1 = this
# machine only, i.e. phones reach it over the tailnet and nothing else.
#SQUIRE_BIND=0.0.0.0
# The Keep (parent admin UI) — always published on THIS machine's loopback only:
# http://127.0.0.1:4920
#SQUIRE_KEEP_PORT=4920

# --- The Keep's exposure --------------------------------------------------
# Default: the Keep binds only the container's bridge interface, so it is reachable from this
# machine (the loopback publish above) and from nowhere else — not the LAN, not the tailnet.
# Uncomment to ALSO serve it on the tailnet (administer from your own phone/laptop anywhere) —
# still not the home LAN, where it would travel as cleartext HTTP. It stays behind the Knight
# login, which locks an account after repeated wrong secrets (SQUIRE-T-0130). Do NOT enable this
# before the household has an admin: until then the first-run "create the admin" form is open to
# every device on your tailnet, the Squires' phones included.
#KEEP_BIND=0.0.0.0

# --- Remote access via Tailscale ------------------------------------------
# Joins the stack to your tailnet so the phone API is reachable from anywhere at
# http://<TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME>.<tailnet>.ts.net:<SQUIRE_API_PORT>.
# 1. Tailscale admin console → Settings → Keys → Generate auth key (a one-off key is enough:
#    node state persists in the `tailscale-state` volume).
# 2. Set TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY + COMPOSE_PROFILES=tailscale below, then `angreal deploy up`.
# 3. In the admin console, disable key expiry for the new `squire` machine.
# 4. Install Tailscale on each phone, sign in to the same tailnet, then pair (or re-pair) it with
#    SQUIRE_PAIR_HOST set to the tailnet address.
#TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-...
#TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME=squire
# Extra `tailscale up` flags, e.g. --advertise-tags=tag:squire
#TAILSCALE_EXTRA_ARGS=
# Compose profiles to enable (comma-separated). `tailscale` starts the node.
#COMPOSE_PROFILES=tailscale

# --- First run (FRESH data volume only; ignored once a household exists) ---
#SQUIRE_HOUSEHOLD=home
# The container has no local timezone to detect — set it, or daily quests reset at UTC midnight
# until you change it in the Keep's Settings tab.
#SQUIRE_TZ=America/Chicago
# Optional headless admin bootstrap; leave unset to create the admin in the Keep's first-run form.
#SQUIRE_ADMIN_NAME=
#SQUIRE_ADMIN_SECRET=

# --- Misc -----------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub token for the phone-APK sync's API calls (any valid token; no scopes) — avoids the
# unauthenticated 60 req/hr limit (SQUIRE-T-0117).
#SQUIRE_UPDATE_TOKEN=
#RUST_LOG=info
